{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly. Coffee flavor varies greatly depending on several factors:\n\n1. **Roast Level**:  \n- Light roasts tend to have bright, fruity, and sometimes sour notes.\n- Medium roasts often provide a balance between acidity, body, and sweetness.\n- Dark roasts are fuller-bodied, less acidic, and have deeper, sometimes bitter flavors.\n\n2. **Origin and Processing**:  \n- The altitude and processing method of the beans play a role in the flavor profile\u2014higher altitudes often yield more acidity and complex flavors.\n\n3. **Bean Variety**:  \n- Arabica beans are known for their nuanced, sometimes fruity or floral notes, while Robusta beans are stronger and more bitter.\n\n4. **Preparation Method**:  \n- The grind size, water temperature, and extraction time all influence taste. For example, a finer grind may help reduce sourness, while a coarser grind can make the coffee taste weak or flat.\n\n5. **Personal Preferences**:  \n- Some enjoy the sharpness of a light roast, while others prefer the boldness of a dark roast or even flavored coffees.\n\nUltimately, the best coffee is the one that matches your taste preferences, whether you seek something mild and gentle or bold and robust. If you ever want recommendations based on specific preferences, feel free to ask!", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0011-03-12177:7": 38.87648010253906, "clueweb22-en0035-55-09015:3": 38.73321533203125, "clueweb22-en0035-50-09495:6": 38.4517936706543, "clueweb22-en0044-33-07902:1": 38.30559539794922, "clueweb22-en0043-72-15068:8": 38.138587951660156, "clueweb22-en0011-03-12177:6": 38.12778091430664, "clueweb22-en0038-12-04569:4": 38.10517120361328, "clueweb22-en0023-89-01844:13": 37.870521545410156, "clueweb22-en0023-89-01844:14": 37.57345962524414, "clueweb22-en0004-93-04535:18": 37.09738540649414}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I get grumpy if I don't get