{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Liberica and Excelsa coffees are both valued for their unique and distinctive taste profiles. Liberica beans offer a flavor that can range from earthy and smoky to floral and fruity, often described as full-bodied with a woody undertone. This makes Liberica a memorable choice for those seeking a coffee with depth and complexity.\n\nExcelsa, though classified as a variety of Liberica, stands out with its tart, fruity, and smoky flavor complexity. It is frequently used in blends to add a unique fruity and roasty note, but can also be enjoyed on its own for a more adventurous cup. Excelsa's taste is more pronouncedly tart and complex compared to Liberica.\n\nBoth varieties are rare and not commonly found in the U.S., but they are prized for their ability to provide a unique and memorable coffee experience. If you are exploring new flavors and want to avoid typical sourness or bitterness, these beans could offer an intriguing alternative.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 54.174625396728516, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:12": 53.125885009765625, "clueweb22-en0020-47-18754:2": 53.06303405761719, "clueweb22-en0019-88-13848:4": 53.01642990112305, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:4": 51.24116516113281, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:5": 50.14065170288086, "clueweb22-en0001-37-16016:10": 50.07897186279297, "clueweb22-en0019-88-13848:5": 49.44342041015625, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:3": 48.474945068359375, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:9": 47.73013687133789}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I get grumpy if I don't get my coffee.", "I don't like the taste of tea.", "I don't eat sugar.", "Dark chocolate is the exception to my rule.", "I start my day by drinking coffee.", "I occasionally experience mild acid reflux and prefer beverages that are gentle on the stomach."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 54.174625396728516, "clueweb22-