{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-2_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "There are several classic types of sour wine-based cocktails, each offering distinct flavor profiles and retro appeal. Notable examples include the New York Sour, which features whiskey, lemon juice, simple syrup, and a float of red wine for a visually layered and balanced sweet-sour flavor. Other popular sours are the Whiskey Sour, Tequila Sour, Vodka Sour, Pisco Sour, and Amaretto Sour\u2014each using a different base spirit with citrus and sweetener for the characteristic tartness.\n\nIf you are interested in wine-forward cocktails (where the wine itself is more prominent), options include wine spritzers\u2014customizable and refreshing with just wine and sparkling water\u2014or the Bishop cocktail, which is a creative way to use up less desirable red wine. For a straightforward experience of wine\u2019s sourness without spirits, you can explore naturally tart wines, such as some young Beaujolais or specific old-world reds with higher acidity.\n\nIf you wish to focus on the wine itself rather than cocktails, you might consider tasting different varietals known for their bright, sour notes, or exploring wine regions famous for producing higher-acid wines.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0017-19-06857:13": 32.18825149536133, "clueweb22-en0021-83-07168:12": 31.672910690307617, "clueweb22-en0043-83-04908:1": 31.580663681030273, "clueweb22-en0034-27-15206:4": 31.56691551208496, "clueweb22-en0025-41-14883:4": 31.549022674560547, "clueweb22-en0037-60-09924:21": 31.484882354736328, "clueweb22-en0002-71-06732:22": 31.47782325744629, "clueweb22-en0045-26-08596:2": 31.1811580657959, "clueweb22-en0036-03-04971:1": 30.930583953857422, "clueweb22-en0001-63-07653:6": 30.830921173095703}, "ptkb_provenance": ["My grandfather used to have a winery in Great Britain."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0017-19-06857:13": 32.18825149536133, "clu