{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The H-taping method is highly recommended for supporting injured finger pulleys, particularly in climbers. Research has shown that H-taping is significantly more effective than other methods, such as X-taping or circular taping, at keeping the tendons close to the bone and increasing crimping strength during climbing. This technique provides targeted support, reduces tendon load, and helps immobilize the affected joint, thus promoting a safer recovery.\n\nTo apply H-tape, cut a strip of rigid athletic tape and shape it into an \u201cH\u201d by making two lengthwise cuts at each end, leaving a solid center section. Place the solid center of the tape over the injured pulley area (usually the front of the finger), and wrap the four \u201clegs\u201d around the finger\u2014two above and two below the joint. This approach stabilizes the area without fully restricting circulation or movement of the entire finger.\n\nIt is important to retape regularly, as tape can loosen during climbing. Remember, H-taping should only be used on injured fingers; preventative taping on healthy fingers is ineffective and may even increase the risk of injury.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 24.09430694580078, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 24.031957626342773, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 23.518230438232422, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 23.330739974975586, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 23.01320457458496, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 22.813920974731445, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 22.280895233154297, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14": 21.650104522705078, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 21.034582138061523, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:4": 20.914701461791992}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 24.09430694580078, "clueweb22-en0