{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It is not recommended to tape healthy fingers as a preventative measure when training. Preventative taping of uninjured fingers has been shown to be ineffective and may actually be harmful, as it can impede natural finger strength development. Taping should be reserved for injured or recovering fingers to provide support and protection\u2014especially using methods like H-taping, which are most effective for supporting injured pulleys and keeping tendons close to the bone.\n\nFor your recovery, focus on taping only the affected finger during climbing sessions, and avoid taping during practice or non-climbing activities to allow your muscles and tendons to regain their natural strength. Incorporate gentle strength training, such as using a medicine ball, to further support your hand and wrist rehabilitation. Always avoid painful movements for at least six weeks as you recover.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:10": 46.582435607910156, "clueweb22-en0031-25-08597:3": 44.88096237182617, "clueweb22-en0007-93-01745:8": 44.54381561279297, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 43.85606384277344, "clueweb22-en0006-50-11612:1": 43.40077209472656, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 42.80365753173828, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14": 42.189151763916016, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 42.179874420166016, "clueweb22-en0010-39-05297:13": 41.48108673095703, "clueweb22-en0019-33-03699:4": 41.40687942504883}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:10": 46.582435607910156, "clueweb22-en0031-25-08597:3": 44.88096237182617, "clueweb22-en0007-93-01745:8": 44.54381561279297, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 43.85606384277344, "clueweb22-en0006-50-11612:1": 43.40077209472656, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 42.80365753173828, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14