{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You raise an important point. Cold water immersion (CWI) is widely used by athletes for recovery, particularly to reduce pain and inflammation after intense physical activity. Many strongmen, such as the Stoltman brothers, use it for these reasons. However, current research indicates that while CWI may help with short-term recovery\u2014such as reducing soreness between events or after injury\u2014it does not improve long-term muscle adaptation or strength gains. In fact, it may even hinder muscle growth compared to active recovery methods like a gentle warm down.\n\nFor someone like you who prefers warm weather and enjoyable outdoor activities, active recovery such as light walking, stretching, or gentle yoga might be more beneficial and enjoyable than cold water immersion. These approaches support both physical and mental well-being during your recovery. If you do consider cold water exposure, starting cautiously and limiting sessions to around 11\u201315 minutes is advised, but overall, warm and active recovery strategies are likely better suited to your preferences and goals.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0040-69-08760:2": 44.2708625793457, "clueweb22-en0003-71-01187:6": 42.24671173095703, "clueweb22-en0014-94-14969:8": 41.83198547363281, "clueweb22-en0002-97-02818:22": 41.60957717895508, "clueweb22-en0007-15-03893:11": 41.292396545410156, "clueweb22-en0044-53-03307:3": 41.00714874267578, "clueweb22-en0024-37-14830:17": 40.67565155029297, "clueweb22-en0008-86-05477:8": 40.619503021240234, "clueweb22-en0018-63-07460:3": 40.41862487792969, "clueweb22-en0003-71-01187:1": 39.88644790649414}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I prefer warm weather for all my outdoor activities."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0040-69-08760:2": 44.2708625793457, "clueweb22-en0003-71-01187:6": 42.24671173095703, "clueweb22-en0014-94-14969:8": 41.83198547