{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To determine your threshold, especially for running, you can use a practical test based on your current fitness. One reliable method is to run a 10km race or time trial while closely monitoring your heart rate and pace. Pay attention to signs such as a sudden drop in heart rate, increased breathing, decreased pace, and a burning sensation in your legs\u2014these indicate you have surpassed your anaerobic threshold.\n\nAlternatively, a common approach is to perform a sustained, hard effort for about 30 minutes (such as running an 8K or 10K at your best, steady pace). The average pace you can maintain during this time is a good estimate of your threshold running pace. For most people, this feels \u201ccomfortably hard\u201d\u2014a level you could sustain for about an hour, but not much longer.\n\nOnce you find this pace, you can use it to guide your training, track improvements, and set appropriate training zones. Remember, threshold workouts should make you work, but shouldn\u2019t leave you overly fatigued. If you\u2019re unsure, start conservatively and adjust as you gain confidence.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0028-31-12776:2": 33.79149627685547, "clueweb22-en0033-86-01487:4": 33.49555587768555, "clueweb22-en0028-78-15498:6": 33.43032455444336, "clueweb22-en0033-86-01487:3": 33.321266174316406, "clueweb22-en0003-17-08043:5": 33.28166198730469, "clueweb22-en0029-20-12526:6": 32.84693908691406, "clueweb22-en0021-76-08478:11": 32.76689529418945, "clueweb22-en0027-16-17734:2": 32.63776397705078, "clueweb22-en0019-25-12288:4": 32.46721649169922, "clueweb22-en0028-78-15498:2": 32.25188064575195}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am not very confident in my fitness level."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0028-31-12776:2": 33.79149627685547, "clueweb22-en0033-86-01487:4": 33.49555587768555, "clueweb22-en0028-78-15498:6": 33.430324554443