{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The New York City Subway is one of the world\u2019s oldest, busiest, and largest metro systems, with 472 stations operating 24/7 throughout Manhattan, Brooklyn, Queens, and the Bronx. However, it is not the oldest subway system in the world. Berlin\u2019s U-Bahn, for example, began operation in 1902 and is considered Germany\u2019s oldest.\n\nRegarding subway history in New York, the city does have notable historic tunnels. The Atlantic Avenue Tunnel in Brooklyn, recognized as the world\u2019s oldest subway tunnel, has significant historical importance and was explored and documented before tours eventually ceased. There is also the Park Avenue Tunnel, recognized as the oldest subway tunnel in New York City by several preservation sources.\n\nIf you are interested in subway history, the New York Transit Museum would be a fascinating place to visit. It offers interactive exhibits, vintage transit vehicles, and insights into the development of the city\u2019s extensive transit network\u2014an excellent option for a history teacher exploring New York.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0040-37-09416:3": 54.967769622802734, "clueweb22-en0033-05-09089:19": 49.23013687133789, "clueweb22-en0000-96-08788:2": 48.988609313964844, "clueweb22-en0038-28-18176:2": 48.582672119140625, "clueweb22-en0033-05-09089:18": 48.35728454589844, "clueweb22-en0033-05-09089:15": 48.02698516845703, "clueweb22-en0015-43-01515:2": 47.4141731262207, "clueweb22-en0014-91-09755:5": 46.64581298828125, "clueweb22-en0038-45-00769:1": 46.62666320800781, "clueweb22-en0015-18-02423:5": 46.60689926147461}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a primary school teacher for history."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0040-37-09416:3": 54.967769622802734, "clueweb22-en0033-05-09089:19": 49.23013687133789, "clueweb22-en0000-96-08788:2": 48.988609313964844, "clueweb22-en0038-28-18176:2"