{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It is very unlikely that you would simply \"run out\" of milk for your baby. Breast milk production works on a supply-and-demand basis: the more frequently your baby breastfeeds, the more milk your body is signaled to produce. The hormones prolactin and oxytocin play important roles in both creating milk and releasing it.\n\nHowever, milk supply can decrease if there are long gaps between feedings or if you regularly supplement with bottles instead of breastfeeding directly. Some women may face challenges such as insufficient supply, pain, stress, or latching difficulties, but these can often be addressed with support and adjustments.\n\nEnsuring you eat enough and stay hydrated is also important, as your body uses your food and fluids to make milk. If you ever feel that your baby isn\u2019t getting enough milk or you have concerns about your supply, consult a healthcare professional or lactation consultant for guidance and reassurance.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0018-87-03256:16": 27.521642684936523, "clueweb22-en0003-33-15776:5": 26.636287689208984, "clueweb22-en0010-04-05457:6": 26.636287689208984, "clueweb22-en0012-10-05278:9": 26.32477378845215, "clueweb22-en0012-10-05278:10": 26.24773597717285, "clueweb22-en0024-25-18312:12": 26.233909606933594, "clueweb22-en0041-35-06877:8": 26.04825210571289, "clueweb22-en0019-16-05488:3": 25.996353149414062, "clueweb22-en0003-05-06876:11": 25.870840072631836, "clueweb22-en0009-38-02157:6": 25.557004928588867}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I prefer foods with more nutrients and protein.", "I am interested in low-carb food."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0018-87-03256:16": 27.521642684936523, "clueweb22-en0003-33-15776:5": 26.636287689208984, "clueweb22-en0010-04-05457:6": 26.636287689208984, "clueweb22-en0012-10-05278:9": 26.32477378845215, "clueweb22-en0012-10-05278:10": 26.247735977