{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It is completely understandable to feel concerned about your baby crying\u2014it shows how much you care already. Crying is a normal part of how babies communicate, and it does not necessarily mean something is wrong, especially in the early months. Babies cry for many reasons, not just hunger. They might be tired, uncomfortable, need a nappy change, or simply want to be held.\n\nIf you are worried about whether your baby is getting enough milk, it is better to look for signs such as regular wet nappies, steady weight gain, healthy skin tone, alertness, and overall growth rather than focusing solely on crying. Many mothers worry about milk supply, but these are the best indicators that your baby is feeding well and is content most of the time.\n\nRemember, responding to your baby\u2019s needs with comfort and care helps build a strong bond and is an important part of being a good mum. If you have concerns or need support, don't hesitate to seek advice from health professionals\u2014they are there to help you and your baby thrive.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0022-36-15100:4": 37.86909484863281, "clueweb22-en0038-42-14880:2": 37.00634002685547, "clueweb22-en0043-40-11958:7": 36.346256256103516, "clueweb22-en0019-98-11070:13": 35.85832595825195, "clueweb22-en0011-81-13253:3": 35.76852035522461, "clueweb22-en0007-83-15673:3": 35.62540054321289, "clueweb22-en0007-65-16004:4": 35.5181999206543, "clueweb22-en0015-47-17412:13": 34.69388961791992, "clueweb22-en0035-37-13460:2": 34.58418273925781, "clueweb22-en0022-36-15100:3": 34.51319885253906}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0022-36-15100:4": 37.86909484863281, "clueweb22-en0038-42-14880:2": 37.00634002685547, "clueweb22-en0043-40-11958:7": 36.346256256103516, "clueweb22-en0019-98-11070:13": 35.85832595825195, "clueweb22-en0011-81-13253:3":