{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Both microdermabrasion and chemical peels can offer visible improvements for concerns like dark spots, uneven tone, and enlarged pores, but each comes with potential side effects.\n\nFor microdermabrasion, side effects are generally mild and temporary. You may experience redness, swelling, mild irritation, or sensitivity, especially in the first few days after treatment. There is also a rare risk of reactivating dormant viruses or minor skin damage if the procedure removes more than the top layer. After the treatment, your skin will be more sensitive to sunlight, so diligent sun protection is necessary for several weeks. When performed by a dermatologist, risks are minimal, but ongoing treatments are usually needed to maintain results.\n\nChemical peels, especially deeper ones, can cause more pronounced side effects such as irritation, swelling, redness, sensitivity, discoloration, and in rare cases, infection or scarring. Recovery time and severity of side effects depend on the strength of the peel. Darker skin tones may be at higher risk for pigmentation changes with deeper peels. Like microdermabrasion, strict sun protection and gentle skin care are essential during recovery.\n\nBoth treatments require careful ingredient review due to your nut allergy. Overall, most side effects are mild and temporary when performed by qualified professionals.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:10": 40.97050094604492, "clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:9": 40.26284408569336, "clueweb22-en0036-14-13056:11": 40.116851806640625, "clueweb22-en0000-24-11991:11": 39.84634017944336, "clueweb22-en0000-24-11991:12": 39.41578674316406, "clueweb22-en0025-19-00053:6": 37.87944030761719, "clueweb22-en0032-47-03490:7": 37.688018798828125, "clueweb22-en0004-95-05610:12": 37.01890182495117, "clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:5": 36.857696533203125, "clueweb22