{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly. The idea is to use structured time intervals to help you focus on one task at a time, but with the flexibility to switch when your attention starts to drift. Here\u2019s how you can do it:\n\n1. **Choose Two Tasks:** Select two tasks you need to complete.\n2. **Set a Timer:** Use a timer (for example, 20\u201330 minutes) to focus on the first task. When the timer goes off, switch to the second task for the same amount of time.\n3. **Alternate Regularly:** Continue alternating between the two tasks. This allows you to use your natural tendency to seek stimulation without abandoning tasks unfinished.\n4. **Breaks:** After a couple of cycles, take a short break to reset.\n\nThis method combines focused work with variety, which can make it easier to sustain attention and reduce the urge to jump to unrelated activities. Tools like phone timers or scheduling apps can help you keep track of intervals and switch tasks smoothly.\n\nWould you like help setting up a sample schedule for your current workload?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0001-38-03237:5": 24.40671157836914, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:2": 23.572771072387695, "clueweb22-en0045-19-12715:8": 23.510522842407227, "clueweb22-en0029-26-11797:4": 23.204145431518555, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 22.99199867248535, "clueweb22-en0026-92-00831:3": 22.709264755249023, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:8": 22.676715850830078, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:3": 22.67346954345703, "clueweb22-en0006-96-00949:4": 22.615507125854492, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:9": 22.505619049072266}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0001-38-03237:5": 24.40671157836914, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:2": 23.572771072387695, "clueweb22-en0045-19-12715:8": 23.510522842407227, "clueweb22-en0029-26-11797:4": 23.204145431518555, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 22.991998