{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "That is a very understandable concern. While the Pomodoro Technique offers structure, its rigid timing can indeed disrupt your natural flow, especially if you find yourself in a productive \u201chyperfocus\u201d state. Some people find that this strictness actually becomes counterproductive for them.\n\nInstead, you might consider a more flexible approach inspired by Pomodoro principles:\n\n- **Adjust the timer**: Rather than always working in 25-minute intervals, set your timer for longer or shorter periods that better match your attention span. You can also skip the timer entirely when you feel deeply focused and only use it when you notice your attention wandering.\n- **Task batching**: Choose a single task to focus on until you feel your concentration fading, then take a short break or switch tasks. This honors your natural focus patterns without external interruption.\n- **Meaningful breaks**: Even with a sedentary lifestyle, use your breaks to stand up, stretch, or briefly step away from your workspace. This can help recharge your mind without disrupting your flow.\n- **Communicate your needs**: Let colleagues know about your preferred way of working, so you can protect your quiet, focused environment.\n\nThe key is to use timers and breaks as tools, not strict rules\u2014adapt them to fit your personal productivity rhythms.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:21": 71.0709457397461, "clueweb22-en0010-71-10871:15": 69.48384094238281, "clueweb22-en0010-55-02906:3": 69.23500061035156, "clueweb22-en0038-55-03763:2": 68.63459014892578, "clueweb22-en0001-49-04668:16": 68.43350219726562, "clueweb22-en0003-44-15078:12": 67.9294204711914, "clueweb22-en0015-27-05231:11": 67.6754150390625, "clueweb22-en0005-54-19421:11": 67.56439971923828, "clueweb22-en0011-92-19024:10": 67.51485443115234, "clueweb22-en0004-59-16742:12"