{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Thank you for clarifying. Meetings can indeed be a significant source of distraction, especially when you are in a state of deep focus or hyperfocus. Even in a quiet office, being pulled out of your workflow for a meeting can disrupt your attention and make it difficult to regain momentum afterward.\n\nTo minimize the impact of meetings as distractions, consider the following strategies:\n\n- Block out focused work time on your calendar so colleagues know when you prefer not to be interrupted.  \n- If possible, request that meetings be scheduled in batches or at times when your energy and focus are naturally lower, preserving your peak focus periods for important tasks.\n- Before each meeting, take a few moments to jot down what you were working on. This makes it easier to return to your task afterward.\n- After the meeting, give yourself a short transition period to review your notes and reorient yourself before diving back into focused work.\n\nThese approaches can help you protect your attention and maintain productivity, even when meetings are necessary parts of your workday.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0020-78-10594:14": 33.84560775756836, "clueweb22-en0023-18-01227:13": 33.246891021728516, "clueweb22-en0014-90-13549:13": 32.81450653076172, "clueweb22-en0032-48-08864:7": 32.413597106933594, "clueweb22-en0033-68-02460:14": 32.35567092895508, "clueweb22-en0002-13-18940:12": 32.284305572509766, "clueweb22-en0030-54-15087:3": 32.250675201416016, "clueweb22-en0032-18-03467:8": 32.18034362792969, "clueweb22-en0030-05-00631:2": 32.13228988647461, "clueweb22-en0036-30-15322:2": 31.95472526550293}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I love it when it is quiet.", "I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle.", "I can sit the entire day without feeling physical pain."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0020-78-10594:14": 33.8456077575