{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly. Tattoo needles come in various types and configurations, each designed for specific effects and techniques. The most common types you\u2019ll encounter are:\n\n- Liner needles: Used for outlining designs. They group the needles in a tight, circular formation to create precise, clean lines.\n- Shader needles: Arranged in a looser, wider formation, these are used for shading and coloring in larger areas.\n- Magnum needles: These are flat and wide, ideal for filling and shading large sections smoothly.\n\nEach needle type comes in different sizes, which affects the thickness of the line or the amount of ink deposited. As a beginner, starter kits often include a range of sterilized needles for both outlining and shading practice.\n\nAlways use new, sterile needles for each session\u2014even on fake skin\u2014to maintain safe and hygienic practices. Pair your needle choice with FDA-approved inks and proper protective gear, such as gloves and aprons, as part of your setup. If you need guidance on choosing the right needle size for specific techniques, let me know!", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:15": 39.131103515625, "clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:7": 38.58302688598633, "clueweb22-en0021-60-02259:5": 38.27946090698242, "clueweb22-en0026-48-19463:10": 37.81608200073242, "clueweb22-en0022-28-12086:14": 36.458248138427734, "clueweb22-en0021-60-02259:6": 36.44792938232422, "clueweb22-en0039-65-13482:13": 36.37974548339844, "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:14": 36.303192138671875, "clueweb22-en0040-52-03134:1": 36.03153991699219, "clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:21": 35.876529693603516}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I can draw well."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:15": 39.131103515625, "clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:7": 38.58302688598633, "clueweb22-en0021-60-02259:5": 38.27946090698242, "clueweb22-en0026-48-19463:10": 37.8