{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "When upgrading your pedals, especially as a casual rider who values comfort and durability, there are a few key factors to keep in mind:\n\n1. **Material**: Metallic pedals (aluminum or magnesium) are more durable than plastic, especially for rough and wet conditions. They resist wear and provide better grip over time.\n\n2. **Grip & Stability**: Look for pedals with adjustable or replaceable traction pins. These pins enhance foot stability, crucial for rough or muddy trails, and prevent slipping\u2014especially in rainy or forested environments.\n\n3. **Platform Size & Shape**: A wide, flat platform offers more comfort and control, making it easier to keep your foot stable on uneven terrain. Concave or flat-convex designs can further improve grip.\n\n4. **Easy Maintenance & Sustainability**: Choose pedals with replaceable parts, so you can prolong their lifespan and reduce waste\u2014important given your preference for sustainability.\n\n5. **Weather Resistance**: Ensure the pedals are designed to handle wet conditions, as you ride even in the rain.\n\nBy focusing on these aspects, you\u2019ll find pedals that improve comfort, grip, and durability\u2014without unnecessary complexity or waste.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0023-57-01381:4": 35.44596481323242, "clueweb22-en0013-75-07652:6": 35.2170295715332, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:7": 35.07429122924805, "clueweb22-en0000-91-01807:2": 34.5744514465332, "clueweb22-en0016-87-16080:6": 33.76301574707031, "clueweb22-en0019-39-04607:10": 32.723114013671875, "clueweb22-en0002-48-15917:12": 32.572547912597656, "clueweb22-en0030-51-01232:11": 32.56166076660156, "clueweb22-en0005-90-09358:7": 32.51545715332031, "clueweb22-en0001-01-08562:13": 32.363407135009766}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I value comfort over speed.", "I care about sustainability and avoiding waste.", "I'm a casual b