{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Clipless pedals do offer advantages, particularly in efficiency and foot stability, and are preferred by riders focused on performance or long-distance training. However, for casual riders who value comfort and frequently ride on rough or hilly paths, flat pedals are often more suitable. Flat pedals allow you to quickly remove your feet, which is helpful on technical or slippery terrain and in city traffic. They are also less demanding technically, which can be important if you find too many choices overwhelming or if you often ride in wet forest conditions where quick foot release is a safety advantage.\n\nClipless pedals require special shoes and a learning period to get used to clipping in and out, which some riders find intimidating. Many people stop using them if they choose the wrong type or don't fully understand how they work. Hybrid pedals, which combine both flat and clipless features, exist but add complexity.\n\nGiven your focus on comfort, casual riding, and varied terrain, high-quality flat pedals with good grip and support may be the best option for you. If you\u2019d like, I can help you compare specific models suited to your needs.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0037-60-07465:5": 49.48625564575195, "clueweb22-en0021-36-08429:13": 49.46873474121094, "clueweb22-en0021-36-08429:12": 48.86362838745117, "clueweb22-en0026-14-04520:10": 47.96297836303711, "clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:7": 47.91598129272461, "clueweb22-en0001-22-06023:3": 47.82392883300781, "clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:9": 47.657936096191406, "clueweb22-en0013-39-06496:7": 47.40752410888672, "clueweb22-en0040-66-10035:1": 47.107208251953125, "clueweb22-en0000-09-06499:6": 47.07938003540039}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I value comfort over speed.", "I'm a casual bike rider.", "I recently moved to a city with more hills and rough paths.", "I like biking even i