{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly. Using a chain breaker tool is straightforward with the right steps and care.\n\n1. **Position the Chain**: Place your bike chain into the slot of the chain breaker tool. Align the tool\u2019s driving pin with one of the chain pins you wish to remove (ideally not the master link, unless you intend to replace it).\n\n2. **Drive Out the Pin**: Turn the handle of the chain breaker slowly and evenly. The tool\u2019s driving pin will push the chain pin out. Go slowly to avoid bending or damaging the chain. Do not fully remove the pin\u2014just enough so the link separates.\n\n3. **Separate the Chain**: Once the pin is almost out, the chain will come apart. Carefully remove the chain from the tool.\n\n4. **Reattaching**: When resizing or reattaching, use the chain breaker to push the pin back in, or use a fresh quick link if your chain has one.\n\n**Tips:**\n- Keep your hands clear of pinch points.\n- Work on a stable surface.\n- If your chain has a special quick link, you can open it by pushing the plates together and sliding them apart (sometimes pliers help).\n\nIf you feel unsure at any step, consider asking for assistance, as handling the chain and tool safely is important for your bike\u2019s performance and your safety.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0010-22-02970:14": 41.71290588378906, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:3": 41.115867614746094, "clueweb22-en0010-59-02845:1": 41.06570053100586, "clueweb22-en0023-06-11986:1": 41.052974700927734, "clueweb22-en0033-26-03408:1": 41.052974700927734, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:12": 40.80573654174805, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:8": 40.558467864990234, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:10": 40.349578857421875, "clueweb22-en0038-96-11763:1": 40.33144760131836, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:15": 39.89710235595703}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am not really handy with DIY."]}], "references": {"cl