{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "cosine-orconvqa", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For lubricating your bike chain, it is strongly recommended to use lubricants specifically designed for bicycles. These are formulated to penetrate the chain\u2019s internal surfaces, minimize dirt accumulation, and provide long-lasting protection. Proper bike lubricants\u2014such as chain spray or mineral-based oils\u2014improve shifting performance and extend the life of your chain.\n\nWhile car oil or sewing machine oil can be used in emergencies, they are not ideal for bike chains. Car oils are designed for different conditions, and do not protect bicycle chains from rain, dust, and dirt as effectively as bike-specific lubricants. Over time, using the wrong oil can attract more dirt and lead to increased wear.\n\nTo lubricate your chain:\n1. Shake the lubricant well.\n2. Apply a drop to each link while pedaling backward.\n3. Run the chain through your fingers to distribute the oil.\n4. Avoid excess lubrication\u2014wipe off the excess to prevent attracting dirt.\n5. Let the oil soak in (ideally overnight) before riding.\n\nIf unsure, your local bike shop can recommend the best product for your riding conditions.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0039-07-08566:8": 39.930870056152344, "clueweb22-en0019-98-16645:6": 39.17128372192383, "clueweb22-en0007-00-14608:3": 39.067806243896484, "clueweb22-en0030-04-19030:19": 38.8122444152832, "clueweb22-en0043-15-14227:3": 38.78797912597656, "clueweb22-en0024-04-10077:2": 38.7056770324707, "clueweb22-en0009-30-09494:1": 38.37834548950195, "clueweb22-en0021-76-15035:11": 38.31635665893555, "clueweb22-en0002-63-04266:17": 38.25715637207031, "clueweb22-en0039-07-08566:7": 38.04521560668945}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am not really handy with DIY."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0039-07-08566:8": 39.930870056152344, "clueweb22-en0019-98-16645:6": 39.17128372192383, "clueweb22-en0007-00-1460